      "name": "OMA Regen Practices",
      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "03 · THE PRACTICES",
        "heading": "How regenerative agriculture actually works",
        "intro": "<p>Regenerative agriculture begins from a different premise. Instead of asking what can be taken from the land, it starts with what the land has, and what it needs. The practices that follow are not isolated techniques, but parts of one interconnected system, each reinforcing the next. Together, they rebuild a living universe, and given enough time, the land begins to sustain itself.</p>",
        "illustration_caption": "How nature works 101 — for the distracted modern human.",
        "toc_label": "SEVEN PRACTICES",
